    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 1 : conjuguer",
     "statement": "Mets au passé : « Amina (watch) TV. She (study) English. Boris (stop) at the market. »",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "watch → watched (+ ed)."
      },
      {
       "md": "study → studied (consonne + y). stop → stopped (on double le p)."
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**watched ; studied ; stopped**"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 2 : phrase au passé",
     "statement": "Écris : « Hier, nous avons joué au football. »",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "Hier = yesterday ; jouer = play → played."
      },
      {
       "md": "Nous = we."
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**We played football yesterday.**"
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Erreurs fréquentes",
     "md": "- « He playeds » : **played** pour tous les sujets, pas de -s.\n- « studyed » : **studied**.\n- Confondre le passé simple et le présent : « Yesterday I play » est faux → **Yesterday I played**."
    }
   ],
   "reviewNotes": [
